      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's examine this surprising revelation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Покажи мне свой паспорт, Макс.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Show me your passport, Max.' Barinov demands proof of identity, sensing something is wrong.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Вот мой паспорт, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here is my passport, chef.' Max hands over the document without hesitation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "А почему день рождения в феврале?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And why is the birthday in February?' Barinov points out a glaring inconsistency, demanding an explanation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Твой день рождения не сегодня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your birthday is not today?' Senya expresses surprise, realizing the whole premise was false.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я хотел сделать вам приятное.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I wanted to please you.' Max tries to justify his actions by claiming good intentions.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Ты соврал нам про праздник?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you lie to us about the holiday?' Barinov asks a direct question to confirm the extent of the deception.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я хотел забыть все обиды.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I wanted to forget all grudges.' Max provides his emotional reasoning for the elaborate ruse.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Но врать друзьям нельзя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But one must not lie to friends.' Senya lays down a fundamental moral rule about trust.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Любая ложь — это плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Any lie is bad.' Barinov makes a blanket statement condemning dishonesty.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я очень виноват перед вами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am very guilty before you.' Max expresses deep remorse, acknowledging his fault.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "За любой обман надо отвечать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'For any deceit one must answer.' Barinov emphasizes that actions have consequences.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Правда всегда открывается.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The truth always reveals itself.' Senya adds a philosophical note about the inevitability of discovery.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "За любой обман приходится платить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
